      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 3,
          "section": "Materials and Methods",
          "quote": "According to the manufacturer's instructions, the mold was heated to 850 at 6 min-1 with a one-hour hold period, followed by cooling to 200 in a computerized furnace (KDF-009G, Denken, Kyoto, Japan). Each metal button was arc-melted and cast into the mold using a dental casting machine (CASTMATIC-S, Iwatani, Osaka, Japan). After casting, the molds were kept at room temperature.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
